														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1381774">
									

<p>I've seen it done either way. Grammatically, if you're reading SCP as &quot;Ess Cee Pee&quot; then it would be 'an', but if you're reading SCP as &quot;Skip&quot; then it would be 'a'. Since opinion is divided on pronunciation (and many people oppose definitively establishing one of the aforementioned pronunciations as &quot;canonical&quot; due to the lack of canon), I imagine you're fine either way. Just be internally consistent in an article.</p>

